id: pm-g512pv
title: "GH-680: completed Plan close must transition plan_mode terminally"
description: "GitHub issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/680 reports that closing a fully completed Plan leaves plan_mode executing with no terminal transition command. Define and enforce terminal Plan state semantics across CLI, SDK, and history."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-25T02:06:32.672Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T16:31:56.319Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-25T16:31:55.391Z"
author: unknown
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Closing a Plan whose steps are all complete transitions plan_mode to a terminal state in the same mutation, with no separate command required; Terminal Plan semantics are declared once and enforced identically across CLI, SDK, and MCP; The transition is recorded in the Plan history stream with the triggering action; Attempting to resume or update a terminal Plan fails with a typed error naming the terminal state"
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: Closing a fully completed Plan now atomically records plan_mode completed.
expected_result: Closing a fully completed Plan now atomically records plan_mode completed.
actual_result: "Closing a fully completed Plan now atomically records plan_mode completed. Verification: linked tests, full coverage, static/security gates, and packed consumer passed."
